@hark_labs is much better product than @bot .
It's more proactive and notifies you for most things before you ask. While grok bot didn't even whispered a word after I started using it with premium plan from last 3 weeks. 
I sincerely advise to give hark a try if you haven't yet

Nobody asked you guys to insert your own prompts into our chats, like "Find me the best Black Friday deals." My bot took off on its own and started sending me messages without my prompting. Turns out someone sent a message on my behalf, impersonating me and wasting usage. No one else has access to my account. No passwords have been compromised. No failed log in attempts. So it could have only come from the grok bot team directly.

It's insulting that the grok bot team would impersonate the user by sending the message in our chat, prompting the bot without our permission and wasting usage on something I never asked for.

@poteto @mattyp @larsencc

@allenwalton @bot I do find grok bot to be very proactive since I have it connected to my email and slack (among other things). 

I asked my grok bot to work as a chief of staff, which surfaces things that are waiting for me. 

I haven’t used Dot or Duet though.
